# Mapping from git remote to flow project.
#
# Read at step 0 of /ticket, before falling back to the folder name.
# The key is a substring of the origin remote URL: it survives the protocol
# (ssh or https), the local path, and multiple clones of the same repo -- two
# copies of the same repo therefore share the same context, which is what we
# want, whereas the folder name would have split them or, worse, merged two
# repos with the same name.
#
# A project can span several repos: a ticket often touches a backend, a
# frontend and a shared library in the same move, with types that must change
# together.
#
# <remote substring>                  <project>
# my-org/backend.git                  my-product
# my-org/frontend.git                 my-product
